{"archetypes":[{"name":"sut-line-claim","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan cites specific line numbers in aggregate-findings.sh for the validator strip call and the startswith predicate; if those citations are wrong the new test covers the wrong code path entirely.","prompt_body":"Read `skills/review/aggregate-findings.sh` (or whatever path resolves from the harness's `$AGG` assignment) and verify every line-number claim the plan makes: the `drop_impure_empty_merge_attestation_lines` call at line 506, the blocks+pure-attest rule at line 536, the persistence-strip heredoc at lines 665-678, and the `startswith` predicate at line 675. For each cited location, confirm the function name, predicate text, and surrounding logic match the plan's description of the code path the new test is supposed to exercise. If any citation is off by more than a handful of lines or the described behavior differs from the actual code, flag it — a misaligned citation means the new stanza's assertions may pass vacuously rather than exercising the target predicate. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"rename-sweep","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan enumerates exactly three rename sites for zero_findings_padded_attest; a missed fourth site would leave a broken stub-dispatch case or a stale echo title in the harness.","prompt_body":"Search `skills/review/scripts/test-aggregate-findings.sh` for every occurrence of the string `zero_findings_padded_attest` (with and without the `_rejected` suffix) and count them. The plan claims exactly three sites: the case label in `write_stub_dispatch` (line 225), the echo title (line 691), and the `AGGREGATE_STUB_MERGE_KIND=` invocation (line 696). Verify no other occurrences exist — in comments, in heredoc fixture text, in a Makefile target, or in any related script that imports or sources the harness. Also check whether `skills/review/scripts/aggregate-findings.sh` itself references this kind name as a known literal; if it does, that site is not in the plan and would become a dangling reference after the rename. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
